# Prototype signed-in state

Settings > General > Signed in is a shared prototype setting. It is on by default. Toggling it reloads the open prototype, so the page always starts in one mode.

- Read the state with `window.wefranchAuth.isSignedIn()`. Never read the `wefranch:signed-in` storage key directly.
- Read the state once when rendering or bootstrapping. No change listener is needed.
- Use `data-signed-in-only` and `data-signed-out-only` for simple show/hide in markup (for example a Sign in button). Use `html.is-signed-out` for other styling.
- Build sign-in prompts and blocking modals with `createProtoModal()`, following the proto-modals rule. A prompt's Sign in action calls `wefranchAuth.setSignedIn(true)`.
- To gate a whole prototype, check `isSignedIn()` during bootstrap and show the prompt instead of the main view.
